==German==

===Etymology===
Originally called {{etyl|en|de}} ''[[cake]]s'' by Hermann Bahlsen, who brought the idea to Germany in 1889. From 1911 his company changed the name of the article to ''Keks'', back then the plural was ''Keks'' too.

===Noun===
'''Keks''' {{m}} or {{n}} (''plural'' '''[[Kekse]]''')

# A [[cookie]].

